\end{aligned}
\]

1 mark for quotient law

1 mark for exponential form

2 marks

Method 2
\[
\begin{aligned}
\log (2 x+1) & =\log (x-2)+\log 10 \\
\log (2 x+1) & =\log (10(x-2)) \\
2 x+1 & =10(x-2) \\
2 x+1 & =10 x-20 \\
21 & =8 x \\
x & =\frac{21}{8}
\end{aligned}
\]
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for logarithmic form
1 mark for product law
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for equating arguments

2 marks

